    "ordinal_step": 10,
    "$ordinal_step_comment": "The step is recorded so the gap between consecutive stages is itself declared metadata: a stage admitted between two others takes an ordinal in the gap and no existing ordinal moves.",
    "reentry_semantics": "A node carrying `reenters` re-enters the graph at the named node. Re-entry is NOT a dependency edge: it is the constitutional statement that the lifecycle does not terminate (AUTH-INF-001 CR-INF-001 Ω∞ non-terminality). Recording it as an edge would make the graph cyclic and unorderable; recording it as a property keeps the graph orderable AND non-terminal."
